course: dictionary
lesson: 6650
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «number» has more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one. In «the number of children in the class is 28», number means an amount, how many there are. In «her phone number», it means the code you dial to call her.
explain: Read the words next to the word first. «A number of» is different again: «A number of children missed the bus» means some children, several of them, not an exact count. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Number can also be a verb. «Number the pages from one to ten» means give each page a number, in order. The same spelling can be a noun in one sentence and a verb in the next, so the rest of the sentence shows you which one it is.
fact: A number tells how many or how much, like 3 or 12.
fact: A number is a written sign for an amount, such as the number 7.
fact: «A number of» means some or several, as in «a number of children».
fact: To number is to give numbers to things in order, as in «number the pages».
fact: In the UK and Ireland the emergency number is 999 or 112; in Australia it is 000.
exercise: «A loaf has a set number of slices, and a shop sells only whole loaves.» In this sentence, what does number mean? | A code you dial to call the shop | To give numbers to things in order | A song in a show | *An amount, how many slices there are
exercise: «A number of children missed the bus.» What does «a number of» mean? | *Some children, several of them | A song sung by children | Exactly one child | The bus number
exercise: «Number the pages from one to ten.» What does number mean here? | A phone number | *To give numbers to things in order | To add up a long list | A piece of music
test: «The band sang a catchy number in the show.» What does number mean? | The code for calling the band | *A song or piece of music in a show | A written sign for an amount | How many people came to the show
test: «Know your emergency number, because it could save a life.» What does emergency number mean? | The number of people in a team | A number that is always even | *The number you call to get help fast | A song about rescue
exam: Which formal word could replace number in «a large number of votes»? | direction | *quantity | colour | trumpet
